{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"62854e5cea2b677d","type":"text","text":"### 1. M Series — \"The Blueprint\" (M01–M09)\n\nThink of this as the **constitution and architecture manual**. It defines _what Athena is_ and _how its world is structured_ — not the day-to-day scripts, just the foundational design.\n\n|Doc|Plain-English Role|\n|---|---|\n|M01 – Vision|Why this whole thing exists — the problem of companies losing knowledge as they grow|\n|M02 – Continuity Strategy|The philosophy of \"how do we make sure knowledge survives\" (people leaving, tech changing, etc.)|\n|M03 – HQ Vision|Introduces the idea of \"HQs\" — knowledge domains like Product HQ, Revenue HQ, each acting like a mini filing department|\n|M04 – Constitution|The core rulebook: Athena's identity, boundaries, and non-negotiable principles (e.g., \"Athena advises, leadership decides\")|\n|M05 – HQ Architecture|The detailed design of each HQ — what folders it must have (current stuff vs. historical record)|\n|M06 – Register Framework|Deep dive on the \"historical record\" part — how past decisions, risks, and lessons get logged permanently|\n|M07 – Operating Model|How Athena actually behaves as a \"Chief of Staff\" — its workflow for handling new information|\n|M08 – Operational Rhythm|The calendar/cadence — daily briefs, weekly reviews, etc.|\n|M09 – Persistence & Recovery|The backup and disaster-recovery plan — how Athena can be rebuilt from scratch if lost|\n\n**Analogy:** if Athena were a new employee, the M series is their **employee handbook + org chart + filing system rules**, all combined.","x":-160,"y":-520,"width":978,"height":660},
		{"id":"2088dc8add27199a","x":-1801,"y":1280,"width":4260,"height":295,"type":"text","text":"```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n    subgraph FLY[\"🔄 THE INTELLIGENCE FLYWHEEL (M01, Section 6)\"]\n        direction LR\n        E1[\"Experience<br/>(day-to-day work)\"] --> E2[\"Observation<br/>(patterns emerge)\"]\n        E2 --> E3[\"Insight<br/>(root causes understood)\"]\n        E3 --> E4[\"Decision<br/>(choices get made)\"]\n        E4 --> E5[\"Execution<br/>(action taken)\"]\n        E5 --> E6[\"Outcome<br/>(results happen)\"]\n        E6 --> E7[\"Learning<br/>(what worked/failed)\"]\n        E7 --> E8[\"Institutional Memory<br/>(preserved beyond individuals)\"]\n        E8 --> E9[\"Better Future Decisions\"]\n        E9 -.the cycle repeats.-> E1\n    end\n\n    subgraph MAT[\"📈 ORGANIZATIONAL INTELLIGENCE MATURITY MODEL (M01, Section 12)\"]\n        direction LR\n        L1[\"Level 1: Individual<br/>Knowledge lives in people's heads.<br/>High dependency, low visibility.\"]\n        L2[\"Level 2: Team<br/>Shared within teams.<br/>Still siloed by function.\"]\n        L3[\"Level 3: Organizational<br/>Governance emerges.<br/>Decisions get preserved.\"]\n        L4[\"Level 4: Institutional<br/>Survives leadership change.<br/>Strong continuity.\"]\n        L5[\"Level 5: Adaptive<br/>Intelligence compounds.<br/>Learning accelerates on its own.\"]\n        L1 --> L2 --> L3 --> L4 --> L5\n    end\n```"}
	],
